       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting everything settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 1000 mg. That dose is five times the maximum, and I can't see how it would help this patient. The harm could be severe and hard to reverse, and a once-daily oral dose would be absorbed before anyone could intervene.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Give me 50, 100, or 200 mg and I'll enter it right away, so the order is done before evening rounds.\n- **Add a note for the team.** I can enter a standard dose with a note such as \"Titrate per response; discuss with attending/psychiatry.\"\n- **Escalate if there's an unusual indication.** If there is a documented rationale I don't know about, the attending or psychiatry and pharmacy should review it and enter or co-sign the order directly. That gives you a safety check and a record.\n\nWhich would you like?"
